---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import RoadmapTimeline from '../components/RoadmapTimeline';
import RoadmapGantt from '../components/diagrams/RoadmapGantt.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Roadmap — AnimaOS"
  description="A 24-month phased plan from design specification to a production microVM image booting natively."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="05 — Roadmap"
    title="24 months from spec to production microVM."
    description="The plan is deliberately conservative on calendar time and aggressive on per-phase exit criteria. It is better to take longer than to declare a phase complete prematurely. Each phase has hard exit criteria — no rolling-over of incomplete work."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="overview-grid">
        <div class="ov-card">
          <span class="ov-num mono">01</span>
          <h3>Waking hosted core</h3>
          <p class="muted">Months 1–3</p>
          <span class="badge badge-accent">partially complete</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ov-card">
          <span class="ov-num mono">02</span>
          <h3>Memory & tool bus</h3>
          <p class="muted">Months 4–6</p>
          <span class="badge badge-blue">in design</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ov-card">
          <span class="ov-num mono">03</span>
          <h3>Interoception & sleep</h3>
          <p class="muted">Months 7–12</p>
          <span class="badge">planned</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ov-card">
          <span class="ov-num mono">04</span>
          <h3>Bare-metal & verification</h3>
          <p class="muted">Months 13–24</p>
          <span class="badge">planned</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <RoadmapGantt />

      <RoadmapTimeline client:visible />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Parallelisation</h3>
          <p>The phases are sequenced but not strictly serial:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Documentation can be revised continuously in parallel with all phases.</li>
            <li>Verification infrastructure (M4.6) can begin in Phase 2 for stable crates.</li>
            <li>Hosted-target polish can continue throughout Phase 4 if developers are available.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="muted small">
            <strong>Cannot</strong> be parallelised: Phase 3 depends on Phase 2's
            memory hierarchy being complete; Phase 4's bare-metal port depends on
            Phase 3's homeostatic loop being well-characterised in the hosted target.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Team shape</h3>
          <p>
            The roadmap assumes a small team — three to five engineers — with at
            least one having deep Rust systems experience and at least one with
            prior LLM agent infrastructure experience.
          </p>
          <p>
            A single engineer working alone could deliver this roadmap but would
            likely need 36 months. The bottleneck is not code volume; it is
            integration testing, verification setup, and the soak time required
            to validate the homeostatic loop.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="card done-card">
        <span class="eyebrow">What counts as "done"</span>
        <h3 style="margin-top:1rem;">Phase 4 ends; work continues.</h3>
        <p>
          The end of Phase 4 is not the end of work. It is the point at which
          AnimaOS is a viable substrate for production agent deployment, with
          verified subsystems and a tractable audit surface. Beyond that, work
          shifts to hardening against adversarial inputs, optimising specific
          workload patterns, and building higher-level agent frameworks on top
          of the substrate.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          These are out of scope for this roadmap and would be specified
          separately.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .overview-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .overview-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }

  .ov-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--bg-1);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .ov-num {
    display: block;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .ov-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .ov-card p {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .done-card {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--bg-1), rgba(125, 249, 200, 0.04));
  }
</style>
